Z||000000||fiero56||11-01-2001||09:33 PM||||Just got off the phone with Summit. Its official. I have the majority of my engine pieces on (special) order. $1,111.17 to be exact.<BR>Pistons will be tacked on tommorrow(they weren't in their computer). <P>Entire valve-train, clutch(went with C/F I), fasteners, cam degree kit, etc. There is no backing down now. As soon as I have the pistons and rings in my hand, I will have the block machined. .040" seems to be an odd oversize, took a fair bit of (re)searching to find acceptable pieces.<P>I'm shacking with excitement and nervousness at the same time. I'm over a grand into this, and I haven't even orderd the local stuff yet, and I don't even know if this engine will start when I have it completed.<P>I can't wait to get started <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!||||reg||11
Z||000001||Neal||11-01-2001||10:15 PM||||Dont feel bad about the money, youll end up spending much more at the machine shop, I have close to 3000 canadian dollars into my 3.4, but well worth every penny.<P>Its still on the engine stand, ready to go except im waiting for 1 "item".  Real close to two months now, well ill just say im LESS than impressed with a particular fiero business.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||11-02-2001||12:37 AM||||Ummmm, what motor are you building? Are you rebuilding the 2.8 or doing something else?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||11-02-2001||12:57 AM||||It is a 2.8 going .040 over. I don't expect to gain a whole lot over stock in power. But, the plan is for it to last another 180K trouble free miles. That's the plan at least. <P>I've got compcams everywhere in the valve-train, silv-o-lite pistons, Centerforce clutch, ARP bolts in the bottom end, and and other misc parts. The only "used" parts will be crank, rods, block, heads, intake, etc. Looking at $350 in block work(the machinest doing the head work is a great guy doing it for free). I figure another $400 or so in bearings, oil pump, etc. I haven't wanted to add up the grand total yet. I will have one of the most expensive chevy 2.8 rebuilds around!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
